{"id":"st377-1","designation":"ST 377-1","title":"Material Exchange Format (MXF) — File Format Specification","state":"active","suite":"377","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st377-1/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st377-1/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"This document defines the data structure of the Material Exchange Format (MXF) for the interchange of audio-visual material. It defines the data structure for network transport and may be used on storage media. This document does not define internal storage formats for MXF compliant devices. The document defines all the components of the MXF file specification including all those in the File Header, File Body and File Footer. It defines the application of Partitions in the file that provide valuable features such as the ability for an MXF file to serve many application requirements and recovery of partially received files. The document also defines key features of the file structure including the Partition Packs, the Structural Metadata, the Primer Pack, the Random Index Pack and Index Tables. The document does not define either the Essence Container or the Descriptive Metadata. Instead, it defines the requirements for these components to be added as a plug-in to an MXF file.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":8},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":8},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":8},{"level":1,"title":"4 Definition of Acronyms, Terms and Data Types","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"4.1 Acronyms and Terms","page":9},{"level":2,"title":"4.2 Simple Data Types","page":17},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.1 Storage order of UL and UUID values","page":18},{"level":2,"title":"4.3 Compound Data Types","page":19},{"level":2,"title":"4.4 Guide to the Use of KLV Pack and KLV Set Definition Tables","page":20},{"level":1,"title":"5 Introduction (Informative)","page":21},{"level":2,"title":"5.1 Structure of this Document","page":22},{"level":2,"title":"5.2 SMPTE 377M Revisions","page":22},{"level":3,"title":"5.2.1 In-file version numbers","page":22},{"level":2,"title":"5.3 The MXF File","page":22},{"level":1,"title":"6 Overall Specification","page":23},{"level":2,"title":"6.1 Overall Data Structure","page":23},{"level":3,"title":"6.1.1 File Header","page":24},{"level":3,"title":"6.1.2 File Body","page":24},{"level":3,"title":"6.1.3 File Footer","page":24},{"level":2,"title":"6.2 Partitions","page":25},{"level":3,"title":"6.2.1 Partition Rules Overview","page":25},{"level":2,"title":"6.2.2 Partition Rules Summary (Informative)","page":27},{"level":2,"title":"6.2.3 Partition Status","page":27},{"level":3,"title":"Open or Closed Status","page":27},{"level":3,"title":"Incomplete or Complete Status","page":28},{"level":3,"title":"6.2.4 The Status of an MXF File","page":28},{"level":3,"title":"6.2.5 Header Partition","page":29},{"level":3,"title":"6.2.6 Body Partition","page":29},{"level":3,"title":"6.2.7 Footer Partition","page":29},{"level":3,"title":"6.2.8 Using Partitions to multiplex Essence Containers and associated Index Tables (Informative)","page":29},{"level":2,"title":"6.3 KLV Coding","page":30},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.1 KLV Coding Sequence","page":30},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.2 KLV Coded Dark Components","page":31},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.3 KLV Fill Items","page":31},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.4 KLV Lengths","page":32},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.5 Local set Lengths","page":32},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.6 Variable-Length Pack Lengths","page":32},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.7 Defined-Length Pack Lengths","page":32},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.8 MXF Keys and Universal Labels","page":33},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.9 Constraints on recursive Groupings of KLV items","page":33},{"level":3,"title":"6.3.10 The Primer Pack, Dark Metadata and MXF extensions","page":33},{"level":2,"title":"6.4 MXF Encoding Requirements","page":34},{"level":3,"title":"6.4.1 KLV Alignment Grid (KAG)","page":35},{"level":3,"title":"6.4.2 MXF Byte Order","page":3